---
source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
Rust-native workspace manager for Odoo projects.

Aggregates pull requests, locks and vaults every commit, ports fixes across Odoo series and promotes exact pins between environments, with pyproject.toml [tool.odx] as the single source of truth.

Usage: odx [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  aggregate      Fetch and merge the configured PRs and branches
  lock           Resolve every merge and package to a SHA, vault it, write odx.lock
  vendor         Install the locked packages into the addon directories; write the platform requirements
  build          Build (and publish) wheels of aggregated, unmerged and private addons
  verify         Check that the working tree, lockfiles, vendored content or installed wheels match
  dev            Prepare a local development workspace, or develop one package
  add            Add a repository, merge or package to pyproject.toml
  drop           Remove a merge or package from pyproject.toml and odx.lock
  import         Convert repos.yaml (and addons.yaml) into [tool.odx]
  export         Write repos.yaml / addons.yaml from [tool.odx]
  git-aggregate  Run the gitaggregate-compatible drop-in (same as `git-aggregate-rs`)
  dashboard      One combined view of pinned PRs, upstream changes, ports, updates and drift
  status         Aggregation and upstream status per merge and package [alias: track]
  suggest        Upstream changes on other series that touch your modules
  verdict        Record, list, revoke and share decisions about upstream changes
  check-deps     Compare __manifest__.py dependencies with pyproject.toml
  glue           Glue addons Odoo would install with what the project has, that it does not have
  sniff          List database migration scripts introduced by merges
  changelog      Release notes between two states of odx.lock: merges, packages, Odoo and migrations
  diff           Changes between two states of odx.lock likely to affect the database schema
  stats          Lines of code per language
  upgrade        Module availability and code readiness for the next Odoo series
  port           Port PRs or missing commits to another series; maintainer sweeps; blacklists
  migrate        Migrate addons to another Odoo series, the OCA way: history, pre-commit and odoo-lint fixes
  promote        Copy exact pins (and optionally code) of modules or a feature between environments
  env            List and compare environments
  bot            Upstream dashboard issue and actionable PRs (nightly CI)
  sync           Prefetch the repositories and PR refs of workspaces into the cache
  daemon         Run sync continuously or install it as a user-level scheduled job
  cache          Inspect and garbage-collect the shared cache
  lint           Odoo-specific lint checks with project context
  doctor         Check the local setup: git, mergiraf, uv, tokens, cache, vault protection
  auth           Store or remove forge tokens in the OS keyring
  completions    Print shell completions
  help           Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

  -c, --config <FILE>
          The pyproject.toml to use (a repos.yaml for the commands that read one)

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Override the number of parallel jobs

      --offline
          Serve git repositories and forge and index data from the cache only; what is not cached fails. Local work (git, pre-commit, odoo-lint) takes as long as before

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale. Like --offline, this saves network time only

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

  -v, --verbose...
          Say when each repository's fetch and build starts, and what each fetched and merged

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only on standard error: no progress lines, no warnings
